// REJECTED — G-MODEL-PLACE: an action that routes the `confidential` origin to
// a model COUNCIL one of whose members is placed off the device does not
// compile, and the diagnostic names THE MEMBER. Roadmap item 516 slice 2's
// exit test verbatim (`docs/design/543-model-council.md` sections 6 and 14).
//
// This file is `examples/model_council_binding.rvl` with one word changed: its
// proposer runs on `vast` instead of `edge`. The two files together are what
// makes this rule non-vacuous: the control admits and this one does not, and
// the only difference between them is one member's placement.
//
// WHY THE MEMBER AND NOT THE COUNCIL. A council's members are placed
// SEPARATELY, which is the construct: each names its own `model role` and
// carries that role's residence, so item 514's ceiling applies per member. The
// council's own residence is the MOST permissive of its members', because a
// council is asked one question with one input and giving that input to the
// council gives it to every member. "The council is off_device" is therefore a
// derived fact, and the actionable one is which member derived it: an author
// told only that `Release` may not read a confidential input has to re-read
// every placement to find out why.
//
// The fix is not "route `confidential` through `*` instead". `*` is DEFINED
// not to cover a confidentiality origin (`docs/design/531-model-placement.md`
// section 2.1), so dropping the arm does not place the value somewhere else.
// It leaves it unplaced, which is a refusal on the value side rather than an
// admission.
//
// This file is also the self-host's reproducer for the binding. The gate built
// from `selfhost/lower.rvl` decides a `route model` arm that names a council
// in its model-placement section and spells the sentence below byte for byte,
// which is why the fixture belongs in the census corpus rather than staying an
// inline test program.
//
// expected error:
//   routes the `confidential` origin to model council `Release`, whose member
//   `proposer` runs on model role `vast`

model role edge   on_device
model role local2 on_device
model role vast   off_device

service Answer {
  fn classify(text: Str) -> Str
}

model council Release {
  proposer  -> vast,
  adversary -> edge,
  aggregate unanimous quorum declared on_tie split
}

component Classifier provides out: Answer {
  route model on classify {
    confidential -> Release
  }
  provide out {
    fn classify(text) = text
  }
}
